Z||000000||fotofrank||10-29-2001||01:38 PM||||I have a problem with my '84 SE. I used the car Saturday morning and after several short trips (1-2 miles) the car would not turn over. I got a jump and drove home. About<BR> an hour after I got home the car would not start. The solanoid did not click or anything. A jump didn't work and charging the battery didn't help. No starter action.<BR> Sunday night ,for the h e dubble L of it I tried the car. It started with no problem and  as a mater of fact started twice.<BR> What gives? any help is great. TIA. I don't wat to hear heat soak (could be) but the started was replaced just a few months ago.If it is the starter.....<BR> --<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||8
Z||000001||fotofrank||10-30-2001||10:07 AM||||BUMP||||reg||9
Z||000002||JohnF||10-30-2001||10:17 AM||||It's in the wiring somewhere.  <P>I'd first check the pos cable to make sure there isn't a short to gnd or an intermittant open.  After that, it is possibly a loose connection in the soleniod itself.  When nothing would happen attempting to start, you don't say there was any electricity to the radio/lights/etc.  If not, it is definitely in the batt cable.  If it is, insufficient amps are going to the starter.<P>Just go from there.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-30-2001||10:23 AM||||First check loose/bad connections, clean them if knarly looking.<P>Doesn't sound like it's a heat soak problem if you're only driving it a few miles.  If no problems with the wiring, then the starter solenoid is bad or there's a bad spot on the starter armature.  You can smack the starter with a hammer or something if it hangs up like that, sometimes it works if you are stranded.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fotofrank||10-30-2001||10:40 PM||||I drove the car around the block tonight.  I parked it, turned off the ignition and tried to start it . no go. Got lights, radio etc but no started solinoid. I tried the car about 10 min later anfd it started right up. I think I'll go with loose wires or bad connection. thanks . Any othe toughts? <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||8
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||11:44 PM||||Hey Frank!<BR>Look at the solenoid to starter connection...<BR>It is a copper strap which will break at times...<BR>Look for the large battery cable to be loose on the solenoid...<BR>Bad rebuild? It happens...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||10-31-2001||03:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fotofrank:<BR><B>I drove the car around the block tonight.  I parked it, turned off the ignition and tried to start it . no go. Got lights, radio etc but no started solinoid. I tried the car about 10 min later anfd it started right up. I think I'll go with loose wires or bad connection. thanks . Any othe toughts? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey Frank,<BR>  Heres my 2 3/4 cents...<P>Check your battery cables & all starter wires including your fuseible links.<P>Good Luck<BR>-Carl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
